---
// Diagram: context accumulates across a chat. Each turn re-carries every
// prior turn plus attachments, so the stack grows while your new message
// (the thin cap on turn 3) stays small. Static SVG, token-driven colours,
// labels carry the meaning so colour is never the only cue.
---

<figure class="diagram">
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 440 240"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="ctxstack-title ctxstack-desc"
    class="diagram__svg"
  >
    <title id="ctxstack-title">Context builds up across a chat</title>
    <desc id="ctxstack-desc">
      Three turns shown left to right as growing stacks. Turn one carries a
      little. Turn two re-carries turn one and adds more. Turn three re-carries
      everything before it, so the stack is tallest even though your newest
      message is only a thin slice on top.
    </desc>

    {/* baseline */}
    <line class="c-base" x1="24" y1="200" x2="416" y2="200" />

    {/* Turn 1 - one block */}
    <g transform="translate(60 0)">
      <rect class="c-block" x="-34" y="168" width="68" height="28" rx="3" />
      <text class="c-turn" x="0" y="222">turn 1</text>
    </g>

    {/* Turn 2 - carries turn 1, adds a block */}
    <g transform="translate(190 0)">
      <rect class="c-block" x="-34" y="168" width="68" height="28" rx="3" />
      <rect class="c-block" x="-34" y="138" width="68" height="28" rx="3" />
      <text class="c-turn" x="0" y="222">turn 2</text>
    </g>

    {/* Turn 3 - carries everything, your new message is the thin cap */}
    <g transform="translate(320 0)">
      <rect class="c-block" x="-34" y="168" width="68" height="28" rx="3" />
      <rect class="c-block" x="-34" y="138" width="68" height="28" rx="3" />
      <rect class="c-block" x="-34" y="108" width="68" height="28" rx="3" />
      <rect class="c-new" x="-34" y="88" width="68" height="12" rx="3" />
      <text class="c-turn" x="0" y="222">turn 3</text>
      <text class="c-newlabel" x="0" y="78">your new message</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <figcaption class="diagram__cap">
    Every turn re-carries all the turns before it, so the context keeps growing
    even when your latest message is tiny.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .diagram {
    margin: var(--space-6) 0;
  }
  .diagram__svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 30rem;
    height: auto;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
  .diagram__cap {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    text-align: center;
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .c-base {
    stroke: var(--border);
    stroke-width: 2;
  }
  .c-block {
    fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 16%, var(--surface));
    stroke: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 45%, var(--border));
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }
  .c-new {
    fill: var(--accent);
    stroke: var(--accent);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }
  .c-turn {
    fill: var(--muted);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-anchor: middle;
  }
  .c-newlabel {
    fill: var(--text);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 11px;
    text-anchor: middle;
  }
</style>
